{{also|Smock}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|smok}}, from {{inh|en|ang|smocc}}, {{m|ang|smoc}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*smukkaz||something slipped into}}; akin to {{cog|goh|smocho}}, {{cog|is|smokkur}}, and from the root of {{cog|ang|smugan||to creep}}, akin to {{cog|de|schmiegen||to cling to, press close}}. {{cog|gmh|smiegen}}, {{cog|is|smjúga||to creep through, to put on a garment which has a hole to put the head through}}; compare with {{cog|lt|smukti||to glide}}. See also {{m|en|smug}}, {{m|en|smuggle}}.

